pprox. 2:30 PM - 4:30 PM): More Strolling & Exploring**\n\n*   **Continue your stroll** along Abbot Kinney, perhaps stopping for a coffee or a sweet treat.\n*   **Explore nearby streets:** You can venture off Abbot Kinney onto streets like Main Street for more unique finds or head towards the Venice Canals (a short walk/Waymo ride away) for a picturesque, peaceful stroll.\n\n**Late Afternoon (Optional - Approx. 4:30 PM onwards): Scenic View or Relaxing Spot**\n\n*   **Venice Beach Boardwalk:** If your parents enjoy people-watching and a more eclectic vibe, a short Waymo ride will take you to the Venice Beach Boardwalk for some interesting sights.\n*   **Santa Monica Pier/Beach:** For a more classic LA experience with ocean views, you could take a Waymo to Santa Monica Pier for a walk and enjoy the coastline. This is also a good area for more shopping if Abbot Kinney didn't satisfy all your needs.\n\n**A few things to keep in mind:**\n\n*   **Waymo Zones:** While Waymo's service area is large, it's always a good idea to check their app for real-time availability and specific pick-up/drop-off zones within Venice or if you decide to move to Santa Monica.\n*   **Reservations:** For lunch, especially on a Sunday, I highly recommend making a reservation or be prepared for a potential wait, particularly at a place like Plant Food & Wine.\n*   **Flexibility:** This is just a suggestion! Feel free to linger longer at shops you love or adjust the food spots based on what looks appealing when you're there.\n\nHow does this initial plan sound? We can always tweak it or consider other neighborhoods if you have a different vibe in mind!"
